    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "L A SR works by alternating between three phases: <strong>hypothesis evolution</strong>, <strong>concept abstraction</strong>, and <strong>concept evolution</strong>. In the hypothesis evolution phase, the algorithm uses standard genetic operations and LLM-guided operations to evolve a population of hypotheses. In the concept abstraction phase, the algorithm extracts natural language concepts from the best hypotheses and adds them to a concept library. In the concept evolution phase, the algorithm uses the concept library to generate new concepts that can be used to guide the search.",
